    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear mandate: leverage elite sprint speed and favorable matchups against soft pitching to maintain our competitive edge in the SB and Roto categories. **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) anchors our lineup as the top overall play, benefiting from a high-ceiling matchup against V\u00e1squez (4.97 xERA) where his elite 0.471 xwOBA should punish a high-contact arm. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12) is a mandatory start; his elite speed profile combined with a favorable matchup against Dobnak (5.16 xERA) and an optimal #1 spot in the order provides the highest daily ceiling among our outfielders. **Trea Turner** (77.93) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.21) also represent high-leverage starts, as both capitalize on the significant vulnerability of Bieber (5.23 xERA), who struggles to contain top-of-the-order threats.\n\nWhile **Junior Caminero** (61.00) remains a strong play, we are exercising caution with several marginal options. **Colt Keith** (53.46) and **Gary Sanchez** (49.61) narrowly clear our performance floor, though both face moderate resistance from their respective opponents. The most difficult personnel decision today involved **Josh Smith**, whose score of 33.52 fell well short of our 40.0 threshold. While **Josh Smith** offers utility, the combination of facing a stingy southpaw like Luzardo (3.20 xERA) and his placement at the bottom of the order made him an easy exclusion for today\u2019s roster in favor of higher-projected bats. We continue to track **Christian Yelich**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** on the bench, but their lack of a starting role or suboptimal matchup profiles keeps them sidelined as we preserve daily game caps. **Dillon Dingler** (40.40) is our most precarious start, tethered to the lineup primarily by his position in the three-hole, despite a significant platoon drag against Webb.",
